//! Source navigation and API tools.

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const SEARCH_CODE: &str = "Literal or Rust-regex search of the process-resident content index (backend liveindex). query is required. The first search in a process builds that index; later searches reuse it. is_regex selects the Rust regex engine. glob filters the index and does not force-include paths the snapshot skipped. The filesystem is scanned only when the widened index search is truncated and the filter kept fewer hits than requested. before and after add context lines. max_results and token_budget cap the hits. This searches file text. It is not a graph-symbol search: use query_graph or semantic_link for symbols.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const READ_SOURCE: &str = "Bounded source text from the worktree. Pass label for the span of one graph node, or path for a repository file. A node with no span is an error. start_line, before, and after choose the window around that span or around line 1. token_budget trims the text from the tail and reports what was dropped. This reads the current file, not another revision. Use git_read_blob for an immutable blob. A missing or ambiguous label is an error; pass an id.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const INSPECT_SYMBOL: &str = "Definition, direct relationships, and a source window for one symbol. Pass label, or pass path, line, and column together (1-based). A partial position is an error: path, line, and column must be supplied together. A position with no occurrence returns state UNRESOLVED and does not guess by name. A label uses exact resolution: missing is node not found, and several matches is an error that lists ids. max_references caps relationship edges (default 50, maximum 500). context_lines is the source window. precision and timeout_ms bound the lookup. scip_path reads an on-disk SCIP index and never generates one; index.scip or .scip/index.scip is used when present.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const GO_TO_DEFINITION: &str = "Resolve a symbol to its definition. Pass label, or pass path, line, and column together (1-based). A source position does not guess by name. A label that matches one node resolves. A label that matches several returns state AMBIGUOUS, candidates (up to 32), and candidates_total, and does not pick. Pass a candidate id next. An unresolved position omits definition. A missing label is state UNRESOLVED, not an error. scip_path reads an on-disk SCIP index and never generates one.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const FIND_REFERENCES: &str = "Occurrences of one symbol, from the graph and from an on-disk SCIP index when one is present. Pass label, or pass path, line, and column together (1-based). Supplying only some of path, line, and column is an error. An ambiguous label returns state AMBIGUOUS and candidates instead of failing. A missing label is an error. Pass a candidate id to resolve one of them. Test and classified rows stay out unless include_tests or include_classified is set. The definition row stays. max_results and cursor page the rows. scip_path points at an existing index; the tool never spawns a language server or writes an index.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const CONTEXT_BUNDLE: &str = "Task-aware source bundle with category quotas and deduplication. Pass label for one exact node, or pass path, line, and column together (1-based) for the occurrence at that point. A file label resolves the file node. The position resolves the symbol on that line. A partial position is an error. The subject is id, label, kind, language, and span. Relationship rows match compact get_neighbors. intent (callers, callees, imports, types, why) biases which related files are kept, so a large fan-in cannot hide one callee. max_related defaults to 10. max_references caps edges (default 50). max_reexports, max_source_files, context_lines, include_classified, precision, and timeout_ms further bound it. token_budget trims related source and relationships first. The target symbol's own source is never dropped; a budget below that source is an error that names the approximate size. An unresolved position returns the inspection with related_source empty. scip_path reads an existing index only.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const MAP_STACKTRACE: &str = "Map stack-trace text onto repository files and symbols. text is the raw trace and is required. A frame that names a file in this repository resolves when the line maps onto a node. Frames outside the repository stay unresolved. max_frames caps how many frames are parsed. This does not attach a debugger, fetch remote symbols, or execute code.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const LIST_ENDPOINTS: &str = "Inventory statically extracted HTTP endpoints as compact nodes: id, label, kind, language, and span. Omit max_results to return every visible endpoint. Pass max_results to page the list; endpoints_total is the full count. method and path filter the inventory. repository reads a child directory of the launch root and does not move the process pin. An empty list means this tree has no extracted route. It does not mean the tool failed. Extraction includes hand-rolled method and pathname checks, a Next.js App Router file that exports an HTTP method (the URL comes from the file path), a Go struct that embeds Unimplemented*Server (gRPC Service/Method), and a file whose first statement is \"use server\" (ACTION /path/name for each exported function). Page, layout, and route modules stay on their own rules. include_classified adds hidden nodes.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const TRACE_ENDPOINT: &str = "Resolve one HTTP endpoint and return its bounded call path. path is required. method is the exact method, such as GET or POST; a prefix such as PO does not match POST. match is exact (the default), prefix, or suffix. handler_file limits candidates to one repo-relative file or an unambiguous path suffix. A miss returns state NOT_FOUND, an empty path, and up to 25 available_endpoints labels. Several handlers return state AMBIGUOUS and candidates; pass handler_file to pick one. max_depth, max_nodes, max_excerpts, and context_lines bound the walk and the source excerpts. include_classified adds hidden nodes. Dynamic dispatch that is not proved stays unresolved.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const TRACE_API_CONTRACT: &str = "Cross-repository HTTP, GraphQL, gRPC, and event-transport contract evidence. backend is the provider root and is required. clients is one path string or an array of 1 to 20 client roots. A client with no static call that matches the backend returns NO_STATIC_CLIENT_MATCH. That is an honest miss, and it is not a fabricated binding. transport, method, and path filter the contract. changed_files and client_names narrow the diff. max_endpoints, max_matches, max_impact_depth, max_source_files, max_source_file_bytes, max_affected_files, top_n, page_size, per_item_limit, and cursor bound the answer. response_detail selects the row shape. include_tests and include_classified add those nodes. client_wrappers and auto_discover_wrappers name wrapper modules. runtime_config and runtime_evidence_files are optional evidence you already have; the tool does not call the network. runtime_evidence_max_age_hours limits that evidence.";
